=== tally over the 9 manifests fetched above (corrected) ===
  CORRECTION to the first tally written above: typos-cli carries `include.workspace = true`
  and the crate-ci/typos workspace root carries `include = [ ... ]`, so typos-cli DOES use an
  allow-list, inherited rather than written in its own manifest. raw/opus's "typos uses include"
  is therefore right and my first pass, which grepped only the member manifest, was wrong.
  packaged-file mechanism: exclude (deny-list) 7 of 9 — ripgrep, bat, just, mdbook, wasmtime-cli, fd-find, atuin
                           include (allow-list) 2 of 9 — helix-term, typos-cli (inherited from the workspace root)
                           Cargo default with neither field: 0 of 9
  explicit [[bin]] block: 7 of 9 (bat and atuin auto-discover)
  explicit [lib] block:   2 of 9 (just, wasmtime-cli — both only to set doctest = false)
  package name != bin name: 5 of 9 — ripgrep/rg, wasmtime-cli/wasmtime, typos-cli/typos, fd-find/fd, helix-term/hx
